A||||10||rprevo||88 GT Rims||||9||
Z||000000||rprevo||03-28-2001||11:40 AM|||| I have been reading on this forum about<BR>88 GT rims being different,<BR>is the wider rim look different then the <BR>87 or 86 GT rims?<P>   Ray<p>[This message has been edited by rprevo (edited 03-28-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000001||Oreif||03-28-2001||11:52 AM||||The 88 rear wheels and the 86/87 GT wheels are the same. They are 7" wide. The only difference is the 88 fronts. They are 6.5" wide and I think the offset is slightly different.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Kelvin Vivian||03-28-2001||10:42 PM||||Don't be sad, be angry like me!!!<P>If you look closely in the photo below, the 88 GT has different rim widths, smaller (6in or 6.5in) in front, and larger (7 in) in rear...<P>And if you take an even closer look, the 87 SE in in the background has 86/87 gray GT rims which are 7-in wide at all four corners...<P> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1601741&a=12208700&p=44402874&Sequence=2&res=high"> <BR>||||reg||8
Z||000003||Standard||03-29-2001||12:48 AM||||88 Front lace wheels are 6" wide, and have more offset than the 86-87 because the 88 front suspension is 3/4"(or something close) longer each side.  So the lower offset, combined with the added width of the 86-87 wheels pushes the outer lip out past the edge of the fender.  Doesn't look too pretty.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rprevo||03-30-2001||01:46 AM|||| Thanks, we had had the car apart 3 or four<BR>times between v8 swap and caliper problems<BR>and various other things and never really<BR>noticed a difference untill about a week<BR>ago.<P>  Well thanks again,<BR>Later<P>     Ray||||reg||1
Z||000005||LZeitgeist||03-30-2001||10:08 AM||||Actually, the '88 rear lace wheels *are* different than the lace wheels from '86-'87.<P>Both the '88 rear and the '86-'87 are 15"x7", but the offset is slightly different. If you put '87 lace wheels on the back of an '88, the '87 wheels will stick out about a 1/4" or so more than the '88 rear wheels will.<P>The outside 'lip' of the rim measures the same - the difference is on the backside of the wheel.<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Raydar||03-30-2001||02:02 PM||||LZ, did you take measurements or are you quoting info from one of the online service guides? <BR>At one time I had a set of 86 GT wheels. They were <I>identical</I> castings to my Formula's rear wheels. Right down to the part numbers cast into the back of the rim. <BR>If you have observed differently, possibly the offset was changed part way through the 88 model year?<BR>FWIW, the Spotters Guide gives different rear track widths for earlier and 88 (supposedly wider) GTs.<BR>I question this because the trannies, axles, and hubs are identical for all years. <BR>???????????<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000007||LZeitgeist||03-30-2001||03:21 PM||||At one time, in the alt.auto.fiero newsgroup, I asked a similar question - what I was told was that the '88 rears have a different part number than the previous 15"x7" lace wheels, and that the offset was slightly different. <P>I have a pair of lace wheels from an '87 GT, and I wondered just how much difference there would be if I put them on the rear of an '88 (the Indy II Dad and I have been working on - didn't want to have to spring for a full set of '88 lace rims if we could just get by with buying the fronts and using what we had in the rear... but he likes the white Hi Techs better, so we didn't. However, I digress...). I was told in alt.auto.fieros that, given the offset calculations for the '88 rears vs. the previous years, the '87 lace rims would stick out about 1/4" further than the '88 lace rims. <P>I don't recall where the actual offset info was taken from for each year/part number for the lace rims (I was *thinking* it was from the Fiero Spotter's Guide, but maybe not - I haven't got mine with me at the moment...) But there was definitely a different offset (and a different part number) mentioned specifically for the '88 rears vs. '86-'87's.<P>EDIT:typos<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 03-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||Raydar||03-30-2001||10:33 PM||||LZ,<P>This is probably where the information came from.  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/wheels.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/wheels.html</A>  <P>This is an excerpt from that page...<P>Wheels<BR>General Information<BR>Info - Stock Wheels<BR>WHEEL TYPE               SIZE      YEAR(S)     STAMP  <BR>PART NUMBER              COLOR                 OFFSET<BR>------------------------------------------------------------<BR>N24  Turbo Fin           13 x 5.5  1984        Stamped JR<BR>     10031138            Dark Charcoal         42mm Offset  <P>PX1  Turbo Fin           13 x 5.5  1985        Stamped JR<BR>     10031138            Dark Charcoal         42mm Offset  <P>NX1  Standard Steel      13 x 5.5  1984-85     Stamped TZ<BR>     9590763                                   42mm Offset<P>PC6  Standard Steel      14 x 5.5  1986-87     Stamped TT<BR>     9590723                                   42mm Offset<P>N78  High Tech Alum      14 x 6    1984        Stamped HU<BR>     10034160 (w/Y82 Pace Car)     White       35mm Offset<P>N78  High Tech Alum      14 x 6    1984-1988   Stamped JM   <BR>     10030813                      Charcoal    35mm Offset<P>N78  High Tech Alum      14 x 6    1986-1988   <BR>     10046311                      Gold        35mm Offset<P>N78  High Tech Alum      14 x 6    1988        Stamped XRM<BR>     10104452                      Charcoal            XUY<P>     Compact Spare       15 x 4    1984-88     Stamped RK<BR>     9590503     <P>PH0  Diamond Spoke Alum  15 x 6    1988 Front  Stamped XRP  <BR>     10104414                      Black (19P)         XUZ<BR>     (Made by Western Wheel)                   37mm Offset<P>PH0  Diamond Spoke Alum  15 x 6    1988 Front  Stamped XRR  <BR>     10104416                      Gold (60P)          XXF<BR>     (Made by Western Wheel)                   37mm Offset<P>N90  Diamond Spoke Alum  15 x 7    1986-87     Stamped XBZ<BR>     10049057                      Light Gray     <BR>     (Made by Western Wheel)<P>N90  Diamond Spoke Alum  15 x 7    1986-87     Stamped XBZ<BR>     10054562                      Dark  Gray    <BR>     (Made by Western Wheel)       Manufacturer stamp ATS<P>PHO  Diamond Spoke Alum  15 x 7    1988        Stamped XBZ<BR>     10049057                      Light Gray   <BR>     (Made by Western Wheel)<P>PHO  Diamond Spoke Alum  15 x 7    1988 Rear   Stamped XRS<BR>     10104415                      Black(19P)          XXJ<BR>     (Made by Western Wheel)                    <P>PHO  Diamond Spoke Alum  15 x 7    1988 Rear   <BR>     10104417                      Gold(60P)           <BR>     (Made by Western Wheel)                   <P>Bolt pattern is five on 100mm circle for all years.<P><B><BR>"If I read this correctly, this means that the 15x7 wheel on all four corners of the 86-87 GTs are different than the 15x7 wheel on the *back only* of the 88 WS6 cars." <BR>GOOD POINT! Yes, they are different. There is a three letter stamp on the wheel:<P>XBZ: 86-87 (35mm offset) <BR>XRS, XXJ: back of 88 (41mm offset) <BR></B><P>The 22P book also lists different part numbers for the 88s.<P>However, the 86 wheels that I had were identical to the wheels that came on my Formula. <BR>If you get a chance, measure your 87 wheel from the back of the mounting surface to the back of the rim, then measure one of your Formula wheels. (Or I'll measure one of MY Formula wheels.) Also have a look at the part# (eight digits) cast in the back of the rim. <BR>I'm still curious about this whole thing, as I've heard several conflicting stories, over the years. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000009||KissMySSFiero||03-30-2001||10:41 PM||||one thing on the back of the formula rims is that it has stamped on there  "Rear Only".  At least I am about 90% sure of this.  i know for a fact the fronts have front only stamped on it.  <BR>Raydar--is it possible someone had changed the rims prior to you owning it.  and painted them.  Tomorrow I'll double check on the rear rim since i will likely have them off anyways.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:KissMySSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>   <A HREF="mailto:KissMySSFiero@netzero.net">KissMySSFiero@netzero.net</A>    <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">        <BR>"There's a fine line between love and beer"||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||04-01-2001||09:40 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by KissMySSFiero:<BR><B><BR>Raydar--is it possible someone had changed the rims prior to you owning it.  and painted them.  <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>It's possible, but I doubt it. He sure didn't replace anything else.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>As much "fun" as those wheels were to strip, I'm sure it was the original paint.<P>I've got it inside, doing some work. I'll have a look.<P><BR>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||1
